#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:5
#: ed13fb488ab8444ea96b95b18c48327c
msgid "NVidia TX2 as a Companion Computer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:7
#: 8333aed790514700a83d96ded3cfbad9
msgid "This page explains how to connect and configure an `NVidia TX2 <https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/autonomous-machines/embedded-systems-dev-kits-modules/>`__ using `AuVidea.eu's J120 carrier board <http://auvidea.com/j120/>`__ so that it is able to communicate with a Pixhawk flight controller using the MAVLink protocol over a serial connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:10
#: f01ea333fc0b4d80940741e600b68429
msgid "Connecting the Pixhawk and TX2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:14
#: 9b133b8dfa984be8adeae8d72698cdfa
msgid "Connect the Pixhawk's TELEM2 port to the J120's UART2 port's Ground, TX and RX pins as shown in the image above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:16
#: b3fe3f1086834db5bc88553313d11cc4
msgid "The Pixhawk and TX2 should be powered separately (the J120/TX2 through it's 12V power input port, the Pixhawk through it's POWER port)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:19
#: 8e9a191117554581a3aa5046c058717a
msgid "Setup the Pixhawk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:21
#: a4cc2e9ddb3b47138885f2e05c95fc95
msgid "Connect to the Pixhawk with a ground station (i.e. Mission Planner) and set the following parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:23
#: 6b583977e119406eaed98b12c97d42b7
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_PROTOCOL <copter:SERIAL2_PROTOCOL>` = 1 (the default) to enable MAVLink on the serial port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:24
#: ad1f4ca569cd444799ca1d11a11d2ee8
msgid ":ref:`SERIAL2_BAUD <copter:SERIAL2_BAUD>` = 1500 so the Pixhawk can communicate with the TX2 at 1,500,000 baud."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:25
#: df092b335c1a42e0b9d9f290e05d04ff
msgid ":ref:`LOG_BACKEND_TYPE <copter:LOG_BACKEND_TYPE>` = 3 if you are using APSync to stream the dataflash log files to the TX2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:27
#: d7434e69b47343b3ac04cade58dad86f
msgid "You may need to manually disable flow control on Telem2 although this is not normally required:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:29
#: 83f027c6616f4ab88a1c61b357212b31
msgid ":ref:`BRD_SER2_RTSCTS <copter:BRD_SER2_RTSCTS>` = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:31
#: ef0dc93972d042d98026c108c58671b8
msgid "As a side note the J120's UART2 appears on the TX2 as /dev/ttyTHS1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:34
#: 6d52bb45d10341369011a300b41b2b68
msgid "Setup the TX2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:36
#: 21efe3d95e944ed2a3bacda13a2000dd
msgid "There are two steps required to setting up the TX2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:38
#: b1a855b9a9524adaa13c984f97924c68
msgid "install JetPack-3.3 to an Ubuntu 16 desktop and flash the TX2 operating system"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:39
#: 19f583ac35cd49d390d9619d492b060e
msgid "flash the APSync image to the TX2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:42
#: c66df3f157dd415ebcfd02b6a3a7f908
msgid "Installing JetPack-3.3 and flashing the OS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:44
#: 72ba5d6c82ac49e6b11a44ae3c46b1d1
msgid "First put the TX2 into bootloader mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:46
#: 2a09a9bbf720426ba62366b5de5e6adc
msgid "connect the TX2 to an Ubuntu 16.04 machine using a USB cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:47
#: 869eae57759c4823afdf0223fffe2097
msgid "put the TX2 into bootloader mode by holding the \"Force Recovery\" button (aka \"REC\"), then press the \"Reset\" button (aka \"RST\") and then release the \"Force Recovery\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:48
#: 3d1a159571394bfb84653e412af3c77c
msgid "check the TX2 is in bootloader mode by typing \"lsusb\" on the Ubuntu machine and look for \"NVidia Corp\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:52
#: fadabb9d260141deb49d7e2c7e749314
msgid "Next install JetPack and flash the OS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:54
#: 15e8bc551ae045078dbfd71d15683ee9
msgid "connect an Ubuntu 16.04 machine to the internet and download `JetPack-3.3 <https://developer.nvidia.com/embedded/dlc/jetpack-l4t-3_3>`__ (nvidia login required) from the `Jetson Download Center <https://developer.nvidia.com/embedded/downloads>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:55
#: df01ae3f60d04a8d907bbf39dc748a67
msgid "move the downloaded file to the directory you want JetPack installed into (i.e. \"~/Desktop/JetPack-3.3\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:56
#: f18a40954cc042e8b2e78b4b521e46e4
msgid "make sure the file is executable by typing, \"chmod a+x JetPack-L4T-3.3-linux-x64_b39.run\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:57
#: 77955336e2db42daab4b449439a49f77
msgid "start the installation by running the downloaded file, \"./JetPack-L4T-3.3-linux-x64_b39.run\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:58
#: 67e175053d36485fbbb0d77b223fcd61
msgid "a \"JetPack L4T 3.3 Installer\" window should appear, press \"Next\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:59
#: ce64f6b35a784a0c84525918416d3ef2
msgid "a \"Installation Configuration\" page should appear confirming where JetPack will be installed, press \"Next\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:60
#: b83861d6083a4c3fb12296ad5d336a2c
msgid "a \"Select Development Environment\" page should appear allowing you to select the board type, select \"Jetson TX2\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:64
#: 62a6c4002476403da06fda424139426c
msgid "an \"Installing\" page will appear asking for your password in order to begin the local installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:65
#: 80fe1bc02f7e42878692e583032bf633
msgid "a \"JetPack L4T Component Manager\" screen should appear"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:67
#: cdbb5e1db7994431856f5d71f059e77e
msgid "from the top left, select \"JetPack L4T 3.3\" (this may need to be selected two or three times to work)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:68
#: c0cd29a4f72c49a89f3fc50da10562fa
msgid "for \"Host - Ubuntu\" set the \"Action\" column to \"no action\" for everything (select \"Keep & Apply\" if a question pops up)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:69
#: 99f625bc40b94bd988deab69bd4463a5
msgid "Target - Jetson TX2: mixed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:70
#: dfe21e7b29204038bd89539f5406508c
msgid "Linux for Tegra Host Side Image Setup: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:71
#: ded3530f2a9e443ab34c443dcb53ba52
msgid "Flash OS Image to Target: install 24.2.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:72
#: d764008b91264f9faca8718da0dfdcd4
msgid "Install on Target: mixed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:73
#: 23f8f35ce1f64c2b829fc167e33c4c0f
msgid "CUDA Toolkit: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:74
#: 8aacfb9d72e04bed830bb2375f5ce1e6
msgid "Compile CUDA Samples: no action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:75
#: ffd3bf4364e04f3495be3a721836eb6d
msgid "PerfKit: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:76
#: 43b101166fee4e5c86545c679e46c49e
msgid "TensorRT: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:77
#: 3f1752e7728245a99fe8408e19ef8ff3
msgid "Multimedia API package: no action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:78
#: c2276c4724a34afc8d8d214b5f8a0255
msgid "cuDNN Package: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:79
#: 07ba7b6fefbf4c3383a1eb8f823b6720
msgid "OpenCV for Tegra: install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:80
#: e1001b1244a9490e86a12df420a0d7fe
msgid "VisionWorks on TX2 Target: no action"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:84
#: cc2df8f3e9794de8b932d02b01e2c07b
msgid "an \"Terms & Conditions\" window may appear, select \"Accept All\" and push the \"Accept\" button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:85
#: 2024d64173044ebebfd9a03ea95b6c8d
msgid "a \"Host installation is complete\" window should appear, check below before pushing \"Next\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:87
#: 413507bf295a497285319b2c2ac0a3d6
msgid "At this point, users of AUVidea carrier boards (like the J120) should follow `these instructions <https://auvidea.com/firmware/>`__ to download and patch the kernel to allow the USB ports to work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:98
#: 965e0bb648964d2baad2cc9aafc49d6d
msgid "back on the \"Host installation is complete\" window, press \"Next\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:99
#: 5f42f1360fa14baa87aced0ea536cc23
msgid "a \"Network Layout - Jetson TX2\" window should appear, select \"Device accesses Internet via router/switch\" after first ensuring the TX2 and Ubuntu machine are connected to the internet with an ethernet cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:100
#: a5cd4c8dd8414038b34e6677736d8353
msgid "if a \"Network Interface Selection\" window pops up, select the Ubuntu machine's network connection that corresponds to the ethernet cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:104
#: 24d848904c33450395828548aaf37f75
msgid "a \"Post Installation Jetson TX2\" window may appear, press \"Next\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:105
#: cb230342f32b400d963d193f24738f77
msgid "a black console window titled, \"Post Installation\" should appear asking that the TX2 be put in bootloader mode (this should already have been done), Press \"Enter\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:106
#: 50f694bf8dfc4d1eb2dcfaf9038b66fc
msgid "installation should continue for about 15min and finally a message should appear asking you to close the black console window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:107
#: 6380c01273d6487f9befa7bdd7e4fee1
msgid "an \"Installation Complete\" window should appear, leave \"Remove downloaded files\" unchecked and press \"Finish\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:110
#: f29041903f20416b8115517a63be1d99
msgid "Flashing the APSync image to the TX2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:112
#: da804aea1e5a425081b916366f654d8f
msgid "connect a USB cable from the Ubuntu 16 machine to the TX2 development board, power on the TX2 and put the TX2 into bootloader mode (see instructions above)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:113
#: 9a177fa4667b41dd8bd154b5fdd25d98
msgid "On the Ubuntu 16 machine, download the latest APSync image for the TX2 from `firmware.ardupilot.org <https://firmware.ardupilot.org/Companion/apsync/beta>`__ (look for images that contain \"tx2\" like \"apsync-tx2-201804270923.img.xy\")."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:114
#: 2603c43eb8614d65acbaaf3361a1f581
msgid "uncompress the downloaded image (i.e. open a file explorer, right-mouse-button click on the file and select \"Extract Here\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:115
#: 37805139bf044e85a241c8344c66d729
msgid "on the Ubuntu machine, from the directory where you installed JetPack (i.e. ~/Desktop/JetPack-3.3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:116
#: 4c4a5089df4f413992beb99146c69c77
msgid "cd 64_TX2/Linux_for_Tegra_64_tx2/bootloader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:117
#: 4ce455d81e03424a84a46fec790c7592
msgid "copy and rename the apsync image downloaded above to \"64_TX2/Linux_for_Tegra_64_tx2/bootloader/system.img\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:118
#: 00088d38dd3a4f7f811be7f61f74c21e
msgid "run this command to upload the image, sudo ./flash.sh -r -k APP jetson-tx2 mmcblk0p1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:122
#: 81a354d06c644fbfa5edd014113083f5
msgid "Some instructions on flashing images can be found `here <https://elinux.org/Jetson/TX2_Cloning>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:125
#: 34bc71cc73f04836ac56173f18808b2b
msgid "Notes if using ZED camera or RPLidarA2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:127
#: db43e6e1d11149b4bb4702cde93943f6
msgid "If you are using the `StereoLabs <https://www.stereolabs.com/>`__ :ref:`ZED camera <copter:common-zed>` then the TX2 will need to be powered up once with the ethernet cable plugged in so that it has access to the internet in order to download the camera's factory calibration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/companion-computer-nvidia-tx2.rst:129
#: 8766ee96d51f47ce9edc65fb58193bfb
msgid "If using the AUVidea J120 board, the ZED camera or RPLidarA2 may need to be plugged into the lower USB port to work correctly."
msgstr ""
